{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/552781-using-more-abstract-influences","id":552781,"title":"Using More Abstract Influences","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-13T03:10:26-07:00","id":552781,"title":"Using More Abstract Influences","content":"So, there are some influences which are pretty straightforward to figure out a use for at the 1 and 2 dot levels. Some, though, I'm having a bit of trouble with, at least as far as the current writeup goes.<br /> <br /> Something that exists as a phyiscal thing is easy. 'Fire' for instance is pretty straightforward. Even emotions, such as 'anger' are pretty easy to work with.<br /> <br /> But how do you use influences that aren't so straightforward under the rules? What if a spirit has something like 'Secrets' as an influence? Or 'Knowledge' ? How about 'Art'? How does one Strengthen either of those? Or Manipulate them? Or even Control them? <br /> <br /> How many of you have done influences like this in the past? How did you handle the ones that require out of the box thinking in order to figure out an application for under the base rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T08:12:12-07:00","id":553043,"title":"","content":"For really abstract Influences, the main use of Strengthen is going to be creating the Open Condition, and the main use of Control is going to be creating the Controled Condition. Manipulate becomes the primary way of interacting with examples of your influence - making somene's understanding of a particular piece of knowledge more or less thorough, making a secret easier or harder to uncover, increasing or decreasing the perceived artistic merit of a work, that kind of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T09:22:42-07:00","id":553137,"title":"","content":"Depending on the spirit's concept, one with Secrets may turn people into paranoid messes by using Strengthen. Or make them pathologically secretive. With Manipulate, could cause people to think everything they have in their mind. (I usually allow Manipulate to work as the inverse of Strengthen if the spirit is looking for that effect)<br /> <br /> Knowledge is easy, it's divine inspiration. It's the Eureka moment.<br /> <br /> Art is the projection of emotions thru physical mediums. The smaller the spirit, the more niche that emotion will be.<br /> <br /> More importantly is... A spirit of secrets knows yours. A spirit of knowledge can sniff out what you know. Let that sink in, what kind of antagonists can they make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T09:29:08-07:00","id":553142,"title":"","content":"I've used abstract spirits lots. Strengthen reinforces the action or concept. Strengthening Art makes an artist create better art (adding to their die pool). Strengthening Secrets makes them harder to discover (create a penalty to ferret them out). Strengthening Knowledge makes it easier to remember things or apply knowledge (bonus to recall rolls or to use skills like Academics or Science that rely heavily on knowledge). Manipulation and control are matters of degree but can do things like have an artist paint a specific thing, or make a secret hideout more obvious, or make alter the contents of a book. Remember, the abstract doesn't exist on its own, it only exists in relation to something else. So, the spirit isn't manipulating Art as an abstract concept, it is manipulation a particular artist or work of art. The spirit of Secrets is affecting the secrets a person knows or a secret document or place. The spirit of Knowledge is changing a book, or a library, or a specific person's knowledge. Then moving on to Create gets interesting. The Art spirit can create works of art or make someone with no talent an Artist. The Secret spirit can make the location of a hospital suddenly secret so that nobody can find it. The Knowledge spirit can put new information into a computer or make a random person an expert on a topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T11:42:12-07:00","id":553272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/552781-using-more-abstract-influences?p=553142#post553142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've used abstract spirits lots. Strengthen reinforces the action or concept. Strengthening Art makes an artist create better art (adding to their die pool). Strengthening Secrets makes them harder to discover (create a penalty to ferret them out). Strengthening Knowledge makes it easier to remember things or apply knowledge (bonus to recall rolls or to use skills like Academics or Science that rely heavily on knowledge). Manipulation and control are matters of degree but can do things like have an artist paint a specific thing, or make a secret hideout more obvious, or make alter the contents of a book. Remember, the abstract doesn't exist on its own, it only exists in relation to something else. So, the spirit isn't manipulating Art as an abstract concept, it is manipulation a particular artist or work of art. The spirit of Secrets is affecting the secrets a person knows or a secret document or place. The spirit of Knowledge is changing a book, or a library, or a specific person's knowledge. Then moving on to Create gets interesting. The Art spirit can create works of art or make someone with no talent an Artist. The Secret spirit can make the location of a hospital suddenly secret so that nobody can find it. The Knowledge spirit can put new information into a computer or make a random person an expert on a topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of which is why I love spirits as antagonists. They are delightfully bizarre and the more abstract they get, the more subtly and overwhelmingly powerful they can be. If you want to jump gamelines for a second, that art spirit Eric talked about? Imagine that your Mummy had been carefully building up an area to cultivate Sekhem, but the art spirit disagrees with the aesthetic, so it decides to screw with it my placing random modern art around the area. Imagine how infuriating that would be. Then imagine that the Mummy decided to take it out on the nearest half-spirit, half-mortals they could find...<br /> <br /> Heck, I may actually have to write that up as an SAS! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T19:33:03-07:00","id":553656,"title":"","content":"Thanks, guys! This has been helpful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:29:16-07:00","id":553702,"title":"","content":"Well with strengthen, I'd imagine a spirit could also make something a secret","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T07:13:46-07:00","id":554268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/552781-using-more-abstract-influences?p=553702#post553702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well with strengthen, I'd imagine a spirit could also make something a secret</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, remember that it can only use Strengthen on something that already falls within its purview. A Fire Spirit can't create fire where there is none with Strengthen, it can only make an existing fire stronger. Similarly, a Secrets Spirit can only make something that is already secret more secret with Strengthen. So, it could make a poorly kept secret into a tightly held secret, but it couldn't make something that's common knowledge into a secret. That would take Create.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T23:57:08-07:00","id":555365,"title":"","content":"Yes, quite right, I mistyped there, should have said make something more secretive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}